# Two series, each on a figure of its own. `compare` calls `plot` once for each series, and each `plot` makes its figure
# with one `plt.subplots()`. No value beyond the call holds it (`fig` is dropped, `ax` is drawn on by the body itself), so
# each figure is the call's own: two calls, two figures, named by the step that makes each.

route notebooks.compare
step compare/compare
step compare/compare/plot
step compare/compare/plot/subplots                                  # `fig, ax = plt.subplots()`
step compare/compare/plot#2
step compare/compare/plot#2/subplots

line entry > compare call
line compare/compare/plot/subplots > _·fig@compare/compare/plot/subplots value
line compare/compare/plot/subplots > _·ax@compare/compare/plot/subplots value
line _·ax@compare/compare/plot/subplots > compare/compare/plot value                  # `ax.set_title(..)`, `ax.plot(..)`
line compare/compare/plot > Figure 1 · plot own
line compare/compare/plot#2/subplots > _·fig@compare/compare/plot#2/subplots value
line compare/compare/plot#2/subplots > _·ax@compare/compare/plot#2/subplots value
line _·ax@compare/compare/plot#2/subplots > compare/compare/plot#2 value
line compare/compare/plot#2 > Figure 2 · plot own

home _·fig@compare/compare/plot/subplots compare/compare/plot
home _·ax@compare/compare/plot/subplots compare/compare/plot
home _·fig@compare/compare/plot#2/subplots compare/compare/plot#2
home _·ax@compare/compare/plot#2/subplots compare/compare/plot#2

side entry left
side Figure 1 · plot right
side Figure 2 · plot right
